From 59e2c7075adc6574c6af45326a65ae54f798812e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:32:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: clips to paths, shapes without anti-aliasing, copy
 and clear through OpenGPU

GraphicsContextOpenGPU draws what cairo still did for it after 0077's
paths (cairo-out item 1, gfopenbrowser docs/STEP5-6-WEBCORE.md):

- Clips to paths (clipPath, clipOut of a path or a rectangle, rounded
  rectangle clips) and rectangle clips that are off whole pixels or
  turned are A8 masks, as cairo_clip makes them: the clip so far (the
  parent level's mask copied, or 255), the path drawn into it by
  PATH_FILL with IN (a clip-out by OUT_REVERSE), even-odd or non-zero,
  anti-aliased as Cairo::clipPath and clipOut enforce, or without
  anti-aliasing for rectangles as Cairo::clip and clipOut(FloatRect)
  draw them. The mask covers the clip's rectangle, which a clip-in
  shrinks to the path's box first; a second clip at the same level is
  drawn into the level's own mask. Everything drawn while it is the
  clip goes through it: fills by COMPOSITE_PD's mask, paths and
  pictures under a transform by PATH_MASK, pictures pixel for pixel
  by COMPOSITE_PD's mask (with a global alpha, as a pattern). The mask
  is freed at the level's restore or resetClip, after the batch that
  reads it.
- Shapes with shouldAntialias() off (SVG crispEdges and the like) are
  drawn with stream v1.8's OGPU_PATH_ALIASED, each pixel by its centre,
  as cairo's CAIRO_ANTIALIAS_NONE: gfopengpu.library 0.23 and later
  (OBGPU_CAN_ALIASED, from its version: the bit is a flag, not an
  opcode). Before 0.23 they stay cairo's.
- Copy and clear on paths, and on rectangles off whole pixels or through
  a mask, as cairo bounds them: what is there times 1 - the coverage
  (destination-out of an opaque colour), then for copy the paint times
  the coverage added, the two passes cairo's image compositor makes.

The writer gets the masks' memory from the context (fastMalloc), which
frees what is left when it goes.

Tested on the host (gfopenbrowser tests/test_opengpu_clip.c) against
cairo 1.18 drawing the same calls: clips to paths on whole pixels by six
operators, rectangle clips off whole pixels (plain, scaled, turned),
clip-outs, copy and clear of rectangles and through masks the same
pixels as cairo; circle clips, nested clips, copy and clear of circles
the same away from the edges and edge pixels within 18 of cairo's (two
anti-aliasing rasterisers); an aliased polygon 3 pixels differ.
tests/test_opengpu_paint.c's 408 checks pass, the copy and clear cases
there now checked against the coverage mix instead of handed on.

